  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing eye research capacity and capabilities to tackle the burden of blindness in India: a research-based UK-India Collaboration (ORNATE INDIA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UKRI GROW award - 69 million Indians suffer from diabetes, which can lead to deterioration of the eye which can lead to blindness. Researchers from institutes and eye hospitals in the UK and India will trial a new handheld eye camera and a home blood test that picks up sig</narrative>
